---
below are various notes
-- this project features a slightly new style of code for us [Mia]
  >> && and || 
---- in this style if is preferred over literal and/or (&&/||)
---- this is done as -a/-o are not well defined within the POSIX spec
---- and I have recently changed to make my code portable instead of POSIX 
---- and because -a/-o are not well defined, certain implementations could omit them
  >> variables are named in hopes that they can be understood
---- standard variables have names that I believe make sense
---- variables for internal functions (such as zeroadd and zerogen) make use of __ prefixes
---- this is done to avoid collisions as shbc is intended to be used in complex projects
  >> most of my code now makes use of shbindgen (see github.com/Mia-Rain/shbindgen)
---- shbc is intended to be used as a library of sorts
---- larger projects using shell code are able to make use of shbindgen
---- to generate bindings/functions from refractored code
---- see github.com/Mia-Rain/shbindgen for more details
---

